Chapter: GopHandoff

 The UEFI stub's handoff contract, in one place because two stubs disagree
 about one address and every payload that reads it has to say which one it
 was booted by.

 handoff-magic is the eight ASCII bytes "CDXHANDF" read as one little-endian
 quadword, which is how the stub stores them.

 The legacy cell is option_a_stub.asm's CELL_FB at 0x8000, where that stub
 writes base/width/height/stride as four quadwords. cdx-to-pe.ps1's stub puts
 the UEFI SystemTable at the same address instead, so a payload that reads
 0x8000 unconditionally is correct under one stub and reads a SystemTable
 pointer as a framebuffer base under the other. The magic is what tells them
 apart; when it is absent the legacy cell is the answer.

 We say:

Section: Block

  handoff-base : Integer = 126976

  handoff-magic : Integer = 5063257923364865091

  handoff-legacy-cell : Integer = 32768

  handoff-present : Integer -> Boolean
  handoff-present (dummy) = peek-qword handoff-base 0 == handoff-magic

 The stub writes the header unconditionally but jumps over the framebuffer
 body when LocateProtocol(GOP) returned nothing, so the magic alone does not
 mean these four fields are real. A zero base is the signal for that, and it
 is the same answer as no block at all. Width and height share the quadword
 at +0x18, stride and pixel format the one at +0x20, because the stub stores
 them as four 32-bit fields.

  handoff-fb-base : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-fb-base (dummy) =
    if handoff-present 0 then peek-qword handoff-base 16
    else 0

  handoff-w : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-w (dummy) = bit-and (peek-qword handoff-base 24) 4294967295

  handoff-h : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-h (dummy) = bit-shru (peek-qword handoff-base 24) 32

  handoff-stride : Integer -> Integer
  handoff-stride (dummy) = bit-and (peek-qword handoff-base 32) 4294967295

Section: Boot Framebuffer

  boot-fb-base : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-base (dummy) =
    let hb = handoff-fb-base 0
    in if hb == 0 then peek-qword handoff-legacy-cell 0 else hb

  boot-fb-w : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-w (dummy) =
    if handoff-fb-base 0 == 0 then peek-qword handoff-legacy-cell 8
    else handoff-w 0

  boot-fb-h : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-h (dummy) =
    if handoff-fb-base 0 == 0 then peek-qword handoff-legacy-cell 16
    else handoff-h 0

  boot-fb-stride : Integer -> Integer
  boot-fb-stride (dummy) =
    if handoff-fb-base 0 == 0 then peek-qword handoff-legacy-cell 24
    else handoff-stride 0
